Replay the nested mouse-reporting ladder instead of a single collapsed mode.

mosh does not forward bytes, it re-renders terminal state. CSI_DECSM collapses
the whole 9/1000/1001/1002/1003 class into one scalar, so when an application
enables them together - crossterm EnableMouseCapture sends
1000h 1002h 1003h 1015h 1006h in a single burst - only the last one survives
into the frame and only 1003h reaches the client terminal.

That redundancy is exactly the fallback terminals rely on. Termux implements
1000, 1002 and 1006 but not 1003, so it drops the only mode mosh sends and
mouse reporting is never enabled. Over plain ssh the full burst arrives and
Termux latches 1002, which is why the mouse works there.

Emitting the ladder weakest-first restores the fallback. 1000/1002/1003 share
a single variable in xterm just as they do in mosh, so the last one still wins
and conformant terminals see no change in behaviour.

Dropping the explicit disable of the previous mode is part of the fix, not a
simplification: on a mode change mosh sent e.g. "\\033[?1002l\\033[?1003h",
which turned a working session mouse off mid-flight on any terminal without
1003. The ladder re-establishes state from the bottom on every change, so the
disable is redundant.

Upstream: https://github.com/mobile-shell/mosh/issues/1364

--- a/src/terminal/terminaldisplay.cc
+++ b/src/terminal/terminaldisplay.cc
@@ -304,9 +304,15 @@
       frame.append("\033[?1001l");
       frame.append("\033[?1000l");
     } else {
-      if (frame.last_frame.ds.mouse_reporting_mode != DrawState::MOUSE_REPORTING_NONE) {
-        snprintf(tmp, sizeof(tmp), "\033[?%dl", frame.last_frame.ds.mouse_reporting_mode);
-        frame.append(tmp);
+      /* Replay the nested ladder weakest-first so a terminal that does not
+         implement the requested mode still latches the strongest one it does
+         know. The last mode still wins, so this is a no-op on terminals that
+         implement all of them. */
+      if (f.ds.mouse_reporting_mode > DrawState::MOUSE_REPORTING_VT220) {
+        frame.append("\033[?1000h");
+      }
+      if (f.ds.mouse_reporting_mode > DrawState::MOUSE_REPORTING_BTN_EVENT) {
+        frame.append("\033[?1002h");
       }
       snprintf(tmp, sizeof(tmp), "\033[?%dh", f.ds.mouse_reporting_mode);
       frame.append(tmp);
